	// consumer/fold goroutine), clearing dirty under s.mu. Only the network Insert
	// runs in the background goroutine, and it touches ONLY the snapshot batches —
	// never the hot ring — so it cannot race the consumer's lock-free reads and no
	// longer holds s.mu during the insert (the fold is not stalled). Previously the
	// goroutine ran ring-read + Insert inside HotState.Commit under s.mu, which both
