// tables) in a background goroutine, off the consumer/fold hot path.
// Unlike StartCommit, prune touches no in-memory HotState — it only deletes and
// reorganizes rows already durably committed in ClickHouse — so it is safe to
// run fully concurrently with the consumer continuing to process blocks via
// Conn; the dedicated PruneConn (see database.Store) keeps it off Conn so it
// never contends with concurrent lazy resolves. lowerBlock/blockNumber are
